{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394953-the-devil-among-the-fae","id":1394953,"title":"The Devil among the Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T20:07:16-07:00","id":1394953,"title":"The Devil among the Fae","content":"In many fairy tales and folklore about fairies, there is the stock character of the devil. Examples include The Devil with the Three Golden Hairs, Bearskin, The Devil and His Grandmother, The Grave Mound, The Smith and the Devil, and Godfather Death among many, many others. This is not the mighty evil Prince of this World, or the terror behind exorcisms. He may be powerful in these tales, but he can defied and tricked. He can be met in person, and people can interact with him. Similar versions show up in other folk tales like the Devil and Daniel Webster, the Devil and Tom Walker, and even the musical Damn Yankees. He may be known under various names like Mr Scratch or Mr Applegate. What's the best way to represent this stock character in Changeling: the Dreaming chronicles?<br /> <br /> In his simply a rare and powerful type of chimera? Or something else? Should he be a plot device, or have mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:16:57-07:00","id":1394958,"title":"","content":"I remember there was a project, in the old Shadownessence forums, to create connections between Demon: the Fallen and Changeling: the Dreaming, and addressing this and others topic. I don't know if anything came to be actually released... an Art on infernal imaginery (and actual links) could be great.<br /> <br /> And don't forget the legends about the actual tithe to Hell Arcadia (and the fairies) had to pay...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:24:24-07:00","id":1394964,"title":"","content":"That's an excellent comment. One could take the Devil stock character, and say that the various Changeling lords out there actually paid him a tithe in dross or Glamour or whatever, just as ordinary changelings pay their lord. Maybe have one such character per kingdom or whatever. Perhaps even make that tithe part of some Oath made long, long ago in the time of the Tuatha de Danaan.<br /> <br /> I think any potential links between this fairy tale character and the actual Evil One in other games (whether conceived as the actual Devil, some force of Oblivion or the Wyrm) would be wild speculation, but still interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:26:03-07:00","id":1394967,"title":"","content":"I include a number of Demonic Changelings in my games, Imps, Devils, Shayteen, Baphomet, Deevs, and not to mention I have seen artists portray Firbholg as demonic Gods with human sacrifices. I have a Lilim group of Gallain who are the Demonic Kiths who trace their legacy to Lilith, and I have some Members of the Fallen who underwent the Changeling Way. I have my own Variants of Imps, Shaitan, and Lilin that are different from the ones we got in the books to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:30:19-07:00","id":1394971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394953-the-devil-among-the-fae?p=1394967#post1394967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I include a number of Demonic Changelings in my games, Imps, Devils, Shayteen, Baphomet, Deevs, and not to mention I have seen artists portray Firbholg as demonic Gods with human sacrifices. I have a Lilim group of Gallain who are the Demonic Kiths who trace their legacy to Lilith, and I have some Members of the Fallen who underwent the Changeling Way. I have my own Variants of Imps, Shaitan, and Lilin that are different from the ones we got in the books to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you PM and tell me more? My players deserve to know! (And to suff... have those in our games)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:34:49-07:00","id":1394973,"title":"","content":"There's most definitely a lot of ways that one could go about this.<br /> <br /> Just with the game itself, thallain and nightmare chimera are vicious enough to take up the mantle, particularly Nasties who've got appropriate features. Similarly one could see it as a misunderstanding of Satyrs or Pooka and similar changelings.<br /> <br /> While not canon for CtD outside of the fact the kiths were portrayed in the CtD TCG, the STVault product 'Kiths of Arcadia' includes a kith known as 'Imps' who resemble fiends and are smooth operators who love to make deals with people and always try to get out ahead.<br /> <br /> There are also plenty of fam theories which posit that the changelings of CtD might be closely related to the fallen of DtF, which may have been partially inspired by an old piece of (Victorian?) folklore which posited that fairies were angels that had fallen because they were too bad for Heaven, but hadn't been evil enough to fall all the way into Hell.<br /> <br /> There are enough interesting similarities to make the matter interesting for discussion and exploration.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though I would say that as well as all of these, the best way to represent The Devil could be multiple distinct chimera who occupy the Near and Far Dreaming. Whether regional or cultural, we have tales of The Devil causing mischief from Ireland to the American South and plenty of other places as well.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that most of these chimera operate distinctly from each other, never meeting, except perhaps as an Archetypal Form representing them all who dwells in the Deep Dreaming. One might find Old Scratch rollicking in the Far Dreaming of the American South while Whiskey Jack haunts Dublin Bars and goat legged Satan terrorized the Italian countryside. <br /> <br /> Largely these chimera go about characteristic business in The Dreaming to entertain themselves and fiendish chimera while tricking virtuous chimera. However from time to time, around people of the right mindset, Old Nick might draw closer. Perhaps come midnight in a Louisiana Crossroads, one chimerical avatar can migrate into the Near Dreaming and can from their manifest in Autumn Reality should the right human individual with the notion of bartering with the devil in mind pass by.<br /> <br /> But, these are just a few of my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:49:02-07:00","id":1394980,"title":"","content":"I like @Gryffon15\u2019s idea best, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> also has a good point that you could use the shayateen, a jinn kith from the Players Guide, to represent Old Scratch. A satyr would work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:57:02-07:00","id":1394983,"title":"","content":"There's an Unseelie Satyr in Kithbook: Satyr that would fit medieval legends' about Old Scratch... fit them like a glove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T21:14:54-07:00","id":1394988,"title":"","content":"I have &quot;The Devil of the Crossroads' as a Siochain mantle and Golden Fiddle as a treasure held by one of the local lords who bested him. Just like the Siochain mantle of the Wolf gives some crossover tricks with Werewolf his mantle gives him some tricks that let him dip into Fallen stuff....and between him, Imps and SHayteen there been some sold acceptance that they these are just some wierd prodigals..<br /> <br /> OF course that's innaccurate too... but no one has tried to use Actor on a Fallen and failed yet...after all compare a Fallen to the Hsien....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T21:18:05-07:00","id":1394990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394953-the-devil-among-the-fae?p=1394973#post1394973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also plenty of fam theories which posit that the changelings of CtD might be closely related to the fallen of DtF, which may have been partially inspired by an old piece of (Victorian?) folklore which posited that fairies were angels that had fallen because they were too bad for Heaven, but hadn't been evil enough to fall all the way into Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very old Medieval superstition. Since there was a belief in the invisible people (which every human society has had), the European peasantry had to explain why they existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394953-the-devil-among-the-fae?p=1394973#post1394973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately though I would say that as well as all of these, the best way to represent The Devil could be multiple distinct chimera who occupy the Near and Far Dreaming. Whether regional or cultural, we have tales of The Devil causing mischief from Ireland to the American South and plenty of other places as well.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that most of these chimera operate distinctly from each other, never meeting, except perhaps as an Archetypal Form representing them all who dwells in the Deep Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I'm currently inclined to view it. Kind of like old style Marvel Comics Doombots of Dr. Doom - each one thinking he's the only one until he meets another, and then realizing he is just a servant of the Master. So if he's a rare and powerful type of Chimera, &quot;unique&quot; in a very large geographic area of the Dreaming, what should be his general build? How many points? What kind of Redes?<br /> <br /> I think as a rule, they should be invincible in combat, but never engaging in it. They can defend themselves if attacked, but could never choose to attack because that is not how the Devil works. The Devil can only tempt people, never force them to do anything. But he can be tricked and outwitted, and he always follows &quot;the law&quot; in the sense he operates under certain strict limits he will never violate. And he knows almost everything (although the only way one can learn that safely is to get the answer from his &quot;Grandmother.&quot;)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T21:33:37-07:00","id":1394991,"title":"","content":"I think that each one should probably be shaped to suit the circumstances of their story and how they might interact with the world but any chimera that has grown prominent enough to be referred to as The Devil probably has a great deal of power to throw around, but a wide variety of bans and banes to balance that out.<br /> <br /> Adversion to faith and holy objects, bizarre honor codes, machinations, eccentricities, exceptional luck, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T22:37:03-07:00","id":1395003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394953-the-devil-among-the-fae?p=1394983#post1394983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an Unseelie Satyr in Kithbook: Satyr that would fit medieval legends' about Old Scratch... fit them like a glove.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my idea of using the Baphomet as the Satyr Thallain, or really multiple Thallian for Satyr's, so Baphomet, Harpies, Minotaur, and Kallicantzaros, and Nasty's/Maenad. But the Baphomet will be twisting the idea of Horned Cloven Hoofed hedonists who revel in the debauchery of others, and maybe being worshipped as naughty gods.<br /> <br /> I can Message you what I remember of the notes. I plan to revise and flesh them out in a future project but the Fae Demonic Gallain Group might be half of an over all group of Fae called the Elohim. The Lillim Court would be the one about Freedom and Change. I think I might Use Lilith's three Gardens as Houses, though I was considering before when it was going to be two separate Gallain Groups, one for Lilith's Children and one for the wandering angels, I was going to use Lilith's Three Gardens as the Seemings. I will have it their secret Lore is the First Fae where Children of Lilith from the various times she gave birth to waves of Children, like when she birthed a host of sea demons and invested in each the seed of the Lord of the Garden of Eden below the sea, or when she gave birth to a host of children each with a seed from the Fruit of the Tree of Knowledge. The Fallen know of the Malhim, and the Malhim may actually be the Children of Lilith yoked to fight for Heaven against the Fallen and afterwards they split into the Fomorians (Sea demons ehh ehh) and the Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T23:15:47-07:00","id":1395016,"title":"","content":"Wow. Amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T04:31:09-07:00","id":1395052,"title":"","content":"The Devil Came Down to Georgia...<br /> <br /> Never actually heard it, but it\u2019s like an old country song about a guy who makes a bet with the Devil and wins. Maybe it\u2019ll inspire you guys. (There\u2019s also supposed to be a parody called \u201cThe Devil Came Down to GenCon\u201d where he plays a game of Magic with Old Scratch.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:14:25-07:00","id":1395058,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth noting Kalfu is the Loa of the crossroads and makes deals there and is the Petra Loa aspect of Legba, who is Elegba or Best known to the Fae... the Eshu. So an Unseelie Eshu or an Aithu could be an interesting Old Scratch.<br /> <br /> We could even have a Secret Crossroads Contractors Society or Bannerhouse for Fae who play the role of such soul dealing devils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}